{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-93ca93bda41bce53","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Observation scripts — contracts\n2\t\n3\tThe diagnoser observes the running system only through these read-only scripts. **This page is the authoritative contract** for them; the upstream scripts they were ported from (named at the end) are informational only.\n4\t\n5\tThe Config's `ALLOWED_TOOLS` grants each script as `Bash(scripts/<name>.sh:*)`, and Claude invokes them relative to its working directory (the agent dir, `/agent` in the image). They live in `agent/scripts/` and ship through the Dockerfile's `COPY agent/ /agent/`.\n6\t\n7\tContract source: [[Defect Lane Task Chain]] § Live observation — read path 1 (task files) and read path 2 (metrics). Read path 3 (Kubernetes API) waits on a platform change and has no script.\n8\t\n9\t## How the scripts get their env\n10\t\n11\tThe Claude runner passes only `HOME,PATH,USER,TZ,ZONEINFO,TMPDIR,LANG,LC_ALL` from the pod into the Claude subprocess. `GIT_REST_URL` and `PROMETHEUS_URL` reach the scripts through the existing `CLAUDE_ENV` channel (comma-separated `KEY=VALUE`, merged into `ClaudeRunnerConfig.Env` by both entry points):\n12\t\n13\t- in-cluster: Config `spec.env.CLAUDE_ENV: \"GIT_REST_URL=http://vault-obsidian-personal:9090,PROMETHEUS_URL=http://prometheus.monitoring:9090\"`\n14\t- local CLI: `-claude-env='GIT_REST_URL=…,PROMETHEUS_URL=…'`\n15\t\n16\tAt `-v=2` the runner logs `cmd.Env = [...]`; both keys appear there when forwarding works.\n17\t\n18\t## Common rules (all three HTTP scripts)\n19\t\n20\t| Rule | Value |\n21\t|---|---|\n22\t| Method | `GET` only — no `-X`, `--request`, `-d`, `--data`, `--data-raw`, `--data-binary`, `--json`, `-F`, `--form`, `-T`, `--upload-file`; query parameters go through `-G --data-urlencode` |\n23\t| Timeout | `--max-time 30` |\n24\t| HTTP error | non-zero exit; stderr carries the HTTP status (e.g. `500`, `401`) — curl `-sS -f` or an explicit status check |\n25\t| Missing env var | non-zero exit; stderr names the variable (`<VAR> is required`) |\n26\t| Output cap | stdout capped at 65536 bytes; when cut, stderr contains `truncated` and the exit code is **0** (the cut must not surface as a pipefail / SIGPIPE failure) |\n27\t| Env | only the variable named below; no defaulted (`${VAR:-…}`) env knobs, no gateway secret, no tokens |\n28\t\n29\t## `vault-read.sh <path>`\n30\t\n31\t- One argument: a vault-relative file path.\n32\t- Rejected with exit 2 and no request: absolute path (leading `/`), any `..` segment (`../b.md`, `a/../b.md`, `a/..`), any `?`, `#` or `://`.\n33\t- Spaces are percent-encoded.\n34\t- Request: `GET ${GIT_REST_URL}/api/v1/files/<encoded path>`.\n35\t- Env: `GIT_REST_URL`.\n36\t\n37\t## `vault-list.sh <glob>`\n38\t\n39\t- One argument: a git-rest glob (`filepath.Match` semantics; `*` does not cross `/`; `**` unsupported).\n40\t- Request: `GET ${GIT_REST_URL}/api/v1/files/` with query parameter `glob=<glob>` (URL-encoded).\n41\t- stdout: one path per line; empty when nothing matches.\n42\t- Env: `GIT_REST_URL`.\n43\t\n44\t## `prometheus-query.sh <promql>`\n45\t\n46\t- Exactly one argument: a PromQL instant-query expression.\n47\t- Rejected with exit 2 and no request: an argument starting with `/` or containing `://`.\n48\t- Request: `GET ${PROMETHEUS_URL}/api/v1/query` with query parameter `query=<promql>` (URL-encoded). The path is fixed; no other Prometheus path is reachable. No `time` parameter — Prometheus evaluates at its own now.\n49\t- Env: `PROMETHEUS_URL`.\n50\t\n51\t## `repo-clone.sh clone <repo>`\n52\t\n53\t- The only subcommand is `clone`. Anything else (including `log`) → exit 2 with usage on stderr.\n54\t- `<repo>` accepts `https://github.com/<owner>/<name>[.git]`, `git@github.com:<owner>/<name>.git`, or `<owner>/<name>`. It is normalized to `https://github.com/<owner>/<name>`.\n55\t- Validation, before git runs or the filesystem is touched — exit 2 on failure:\n56\t  - `owner` and `name` each match `^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$` (so `bborbe/.github` is valid)\n57\t  - neither `owner` nor `name` is `.` or `..` (so `../x`, `x/..`, `x/.`, `./.`, `../..` are invalid)\n58\t  - **defense in depth:** the destination `<agent dir>/repos/<owner>/<name>`, resolved to an absolute path with symlinks followed, lies strictly inside `<agent dir>/repos/`. This is checked before any `rm -rf` or `chmod`, and catches a pre-existing symlink under `repos/` pointing outside it.\n59\t- Clone root is fixed: the `repos/` directory beside `scripts/` (`/agent/repos` in the image; `agent/repos/` in a local checkout, gitignored). No env override.\n60\t- Clone: full history, no `--recurse-submodules`, no credentials (public repos only in v1).\n61\t- Replacing an existing clone first restores owner write permission on the old tree, then removes it — so re-cloning over a read-only tree succeeds for a non-root user.\n62\t- After cloning, the whole tree including `.git` is made non-writable (`chmod -R a-w`).\n63\t- stdout (flat `key=value`): `clone_path=<absolute path>`, `head_sha=<sha>`, `default_branch=<branch>`.\n64\t- `git clone` failure (any non-zero exit, e.g. 128) → non-zero exit, stderr `git clone failed for <url>`.\n65\t\n66\tCleanup after a local run: `chmod -R u+w agent/repos && rm -rf agent/repos`.\n67\t\n68\t## Upstream (informational only)\n69\t\n70\tPorted from `agent-sentry-issue-analyzer/scripts/vault-list.sh`, `agent-sentry-issue-analyzer/scripts/repo-clone.sh` (whose `..` traversal hole this contract closes), and `trading/agent/trade-analysis/agent/scripts/vault-read.sh`. `prometheus-query.sh` is new. Where this page and an upstream script disagree, this page wins.\n71\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ea7f4547-d814-4f07-8c73-e3438d2d0206","uuid":"5fd77c2e-d9aa-4c54-9dc4-c8644f537ca7","timestamp":"2026-09-27T23:24:48.991Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/observation-scripts.md","content":"# Observation scripts — contracts\n\nThe diagnoser observes the running system only through these read-only scripts. **This page is the authoritative contract** for them; the upstream scripts they were ported from (named at the end) are informational only.\n\nThe Config's `ALLOWED_TOOLS` grants each script as `Bash(scripts/<name>.sh:*)`, and Claude invokes them relative to its working directory (the agent dir, `/agent` in the image). They live in `agent/scripts/` and ship through the Dockerfile's `COPY agent/ /agent/`.\n\nContract source: [[Defect Lane Task Chain]] § Live observation — read path 1 (task files) and read path 2 (metrics). Read path 3 (Kubernetes API) waits on a platform change and has no script.\n\n## How the scripts get their env\n\nThe Claude runner passes only `HOME,PATH,USER,TZ,ZONEINFO,TMPDIR,LANG,LC_ALL` from the pod into the Claude subprocess. `GIT_REST_URL` and `PROMETHEUS_URL` reach the scripts through the existing `CLAUDE_ENV` channel (comma-separated `KEY=VALUE`, merged into `ClaudeRunnerConfig.Env` by both entry points):\n\n- in-cluster: Config `spec.env.CLAUDE_ENV: \"GIT_REST_URL=http://vault-obsidian-personal:9090,PROMETHEUS_URL=http://prometheus.monitoring:9090\"`\n- local CLI: `-claude-env='GIT_REST_URL=…,PROMETHEUS_URL=…'`\n\nAt `-v=2` the runner logs `cmd.Env = [...]`; both keys appear there when forwarding works.\n\n## Common rules (all three HTTP scripts)\n\n| Rule | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Method | `GET` only — no `-X`, `--request`, `-d`, `--data`, `--data-raw`, `--data-binary`, `--json`, `-F`, `--form`, `-T`, `--upload-file`; query parameters go through `-G --data-urlencode` |\n| Timeout | `--max-time 30` |\n| HTTP error | non-zero exit; stderr carries the HTTP status (e.g. `500`, `401`) — curl `-sS -f` or an explicit status check |\n| Missing env var | non-zero exit; stderr names the variable (`<VAR> is required`) |\n| Output cap | stdout capped at 65536 bytes; when cut, stderr contains `truncated` and the exit code is **0** (the cut must not surface as a pipefail / SIGPIPE failure) |\n| Env | only the variable named below; no defaulted (`${VAR:-…}`) env knobs, no gateway secret, no tokens |\n\n## `vault-read.sh <path>`\n\n- One argument: a vault-relative file path.\n- Rejected with exit 2 and no request: absolute path (leading `/`), any `..` segment (`../b.md`, `a/../b.md`, `a/..`), any `?`, `#` or `://`.\n- Spaces are percent-encoded.\n- Request: `GET ${GIT_REST_URL}/api/v1/files/<encoded path>`.\n- Env: `GIT_REST_URL`.\n\n## `vault-list.sh <glob>`\n\n- One argument: a git-rest glob (`filepath.Match` semantics; `*` does not cross `/`; `**` unsupported).\n- Request: `GET ${GIT_REST_URL}/api/v1/files/` with query parameter `glob=<glob>` (URL-encoded).\n- stdout: one path per line; empty when nothing matches.\n- Env: `GIT_REST_URL`.\n\n## `prometheus-query.sh <promql>`\n\n- Exactly one argument: a PromQL instant-query expression.\n- Rejected with exit 2 and no request: an argument starting with `/` or containing `://`.\n- Request: `GET ${PROMETHEUS_URL}/api/v1/query` with query parameter `query=<promql>` (URL-encoded). The path is fixed; no other Prometheus path is reachable. No `time` parameter — Prometheus evaluates at its own now.\n- Env: `PROMETHEUS_URL`.\n\n## `repo-clone.sh clone <repo>`\n\n- The only subcommand is `clone`. Anything else (including `log`) → exit 2 with usage on stderr.\n- `<repo>` accepts `https://github.com/<owner>/<name>[.git]`, `git@github.com:<owner>/<name>.git`, or `<owner>/<name>`. It is normalized to `https://github.com/<owner>/<name>`.\n- Validation, before git runs or the filesystem is touched — exit 2 on failure:\n  - `owner` and `name` each match `^[A-Za-z0-9._-]+$` (so `bborbe/.github` is valid)\n  - neither `owner` nor `name` is `.` or `..` (so `../x`, `x/..`, `x/.`, `./.`, `../..` are invalid)\n  - **defense in depth:** the destination `<agent dir>/repos/<owner>/<name>`, resolved to an absolute path with symlinks followed, lies strictly inside `<agent dir>/repos/`. This is checked before any `rm -rf` or `chmod`, and catches a pre-existing symlink under `repos/` pointing outside it.\n- Clone root is fixed: the `repos/` directory beside `scripts/` (`/agent/repos` in the image; `agent/repos/` in a local checkout, gitignored). No env override.\n- Clone: full history, no `--recurse-submodules`, no credentials (public repos only in v1).\n- Replacing an existing clone first restores owner write permission on the old tree, then removes it — so re-cloning over a read-only tree succeeds for a non-root user.\n- After cloning, the whole tree including `.git` is made non-writable (`chmod -R a-w`).\n- stdout (flat `key=value`): `clone_path=<absolute path>`, `head_sha=<sha>`, `default_branch=<branch>`.\n- `git clone` failure (any non-zero exit, e.g. 128) → non-zero exit, stderr `git clone failed for <url>`.\n\nCleanup after a local run: `chmod -R u+w agent/repos && rm -rf agent/repos`.\n\n## Upstream (informational only)\n\nPorted from `agent-sentry-issue-analyzer/scripts/vault-list.sh`, `agent-sentry-issue-analyzer/scripts/repo-clone.sh` (whose `..` traversal hole this contract closes), and `trading/agent/trade-analysis/agent/scripts/vault-read.sh`. `prometheus-query.sh` is new. Where this page and an upstream script disagree, this page wins.\n","numLines":71,"startLine":1,"totalLines":71}}}
