{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-884ffc78981c52ce","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Definition of Done\n2\t\n3\tAfter completing your implementation, review your own changes against each criterion below. These are quality checks you perform by inspecting your work — not commands to run (linting and tests already ran via `validationCommand`). Report any unmet criterion as a blocker.\n4\t\n5\t## Code Quality\n6\t\n7\t- Exported types, functions, and interfaces have doc comments\n8\t- Error handling follows project conventions (no silently ignored errors)\n9\t- No debug output (print statements, fmt.Printf) — use structured logging\n10\t\n11\t## Testing\n12\t\n13\t- New code has good test coverage (target >= 80%)\n14\t- Changes to existing code have tests covering at least the changed behavior\n15\t\n16\t## Dependencies\n17\t\n18\t- If `make precommit` fails due to a dependency vulnerability with a known fix version, update the dependency (`go get <pkg>@<fixed-version> && go mod tidy && go mod vendor`) as part of your change\n19\t- No `exclude` or `replace` directives in go.mod (break remote install)\n20\t\n21\t## Documentation\n22\t\n23\t- README.md is updated if the change affects usage, configuration, or setup\n24\t- Documentation is updated if the change affects behavior described in docs/ (notably `docs/observation-scripts.md` and `docs/verdict-gate.md`)\n25\t- When changing CLI args, config fields, env vars, or flags (add, rename, remove, change default), grep the entire repo and update all references in docs/, README.md, examples, and comments\n26\t- CHANGELOG.md has an entry under `## Unreleased`\n27\t- New or changed integration seam (per the dark-factory scenario-writing rules, \"When to Write a Scenario\") → scenario under `scenarios/` added or updated\n28\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ea7f4547-d814-4f07-8c73-e3438d2d0206","uuid":"34c739b8-2953-4c1c-8133-9d126ed04bc6","timestamp":"2026-09-27T23:28:54.218Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/workspace/docs/dod.md","content":"# Definition of Done\n\nAfter completing your implementation, review your own changes against each criterion below. These are quality checks you perform by inspecting your work — not commands to run (linting and tests already ran via `validationCommand`). Report any unmet criterion as a blocker.\n\n## Code Quality\n\n- Exported types, functions, and interfaces have doc comments\n- Error handling follows project conventions (no silently ignored errors)\n- No debug output (print statements, fmt.Printf) — use structured logging\n\n## Testing\n\n- New code has good test coverage (target >= 80%)\n- Changes to existing code have tests covering at least the changed behavior\n\n## Dependencies\n\n- If `make precommit` fails due to a dependency vulnerability with a known fix version, update the dependency (`go get <pkg>@<fixed-version> && go mod tidy && go mod vendor`) as part of your change\n- No `exclude` or `replace` directives in go.mod (break remote install)\n\n## Documentation\n\n- README.md is updated if the change affects usage, configuration, or setup\n- Documentation is updated if the change affects behavior described in docs/ (notably `docs/observation-scripts.md` and `docs/verdict-gate.md`)\n- When changing CLI args, config fields, env vars, or flags (add, rename, remove, change default), grep the entire repo and update all references in docs/, README.md, examples, and comments\n- CHANGELOG.md has an entry under `## Unreleased`\n- New or changed integration seam (per the dark-factory scenario-writing rules, \"When to Write a Scenario\") → scenario under `scenarios/` added or updated\n","numLines":28,"startLine":1,"totalLines":28}}}
