{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b3630e53fccc7746","type":"tool_result","content":"=== go.mod exclude/replace (must be none) ===\n118:exclude (\n=== envparse already a dep? ===\n10:\tgithub.com/bborbe/agent v0.89.0\n=== final config env block ===\n  env:\n    # Live reads go ONLY through the constrained read-only scripts in agent/scripts/\n    # (read path 1 — task files, read path 2 — metrics). See docs/observation-scripts.md.\n    ALLOWED_TOOLS: \"Read,Grep,Glob,Bash(scripts/vault-read.sh:*),Bash(scripts/vault-list.sh:*),Bash(scripts/prometheus-query.sh:*),Bash(scripts/repo-clone.sh:*)\"\n    LOGLEVEL: \"2\"\n    # LLM auth — fleet norm: stateless token via the in-cluster claude-code-router.\n    ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL: http://claude-code-router-dev:8788\n    ANTHROPIC_MODEL: MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed\n    # The Claude runner strips pod env down to a fixed allowlist (HOME,PATH,USER,TZ,...),\n    # so the read-path endpoints reach the scripts only through this channel: a\n    # comma-separated KEY=VALUE list parsed by both entry points (main.go and\n    # cmd/run-task/main.go). Set as plain pod env they would be dropped before the\n    # model ever sees them.\n    CLAUDE_ENV: \"GIT_REST_URL=http://vault-obsidian-personal:9090,PROMETHEUS_URL=http://prometheus.monitoring:9090\"\n\n  # Holds ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN (router token) — teamvault-resolved, see k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-secret.yaml (not yet written).\n  secretName: defect-diagnoser-agent\n\n  # Kubernetes API reads, deferred — see NEXT-DIRECTIONS v2. They need a dedicated read-only\n  # ServiceAccount `defect-diagnoser` (get/list on pods, pods/log, events, jobs, deployments;\n=== CHANGELOG ===\n# Changelog\n\n## Unreleased\n\n- feat: Add `agent/scripts/repo-clone.sh`, the fourth read-only observation script, cloning a public GitHub repo into the fixed `repos/` directory beside `scripts/` and reporting `clone_path`, `head_sha` and `default_branch` [rejects any reference that is not `owner/name`, resolves the destination with symlinks followed and refuses anything outside `repos/` before git runs or the filesystem is touched, then makes the clone non-writable]\n- feat: Wire the observation scripts' endpoints through `CLAUDE_ENV` and align the Config allowlist, image and prose with the four scripts that exist [drops the non-existent `pod-logs.sh` entry, adds `git` to the runtime image, and adds `pkg/scripts/consistency_test.go` to fail `make test` when the allowlist, the scripts on disk and the docs disagree]\n\n## v0.0.0\n=== README section ===\n### Claude subprocess env allowlist\n\n`lib/claude/claude-runner.go` strips pod env down to a safe allowlist (`HOME,PATH,USER,TZ,...`) before spawning `claude`, so a variable visible in `kubectl describe pod` can still be absent from the subprocess. Custom env vars (API URLs, credentials) **must** be passed through `CLAUDE_ENV` — a comma-separated `KEY=VALUE` list set on the Config's `spec.env` (or `-claude-env` for a local run) and parsed by both entry points. Don't expect pod env to reach Claude by default.\n\nThe observation scripts get their endpoints this way (contract: `docs/observation-scripts.md`):\n\n`CLAUDE_ENV: \"GIT_REST_URL=http://vault-obsidian-personal:9090,PROMETHEUS_URL=http://prometheus.monitoring:9090\"`\n\n## Local Quick Test","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ea7f4547-d814-4f07-8c73-e3438d2d0206","uuid":"8814b78c-b63c-4d29-a224-64f96141a241","timestamp":"2026-09-27T23:31:27.229Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"=== go.mod exclude/replace (must be none) ===\n118:exclude (\n=== envparse already a dep? ===\n10:\tgithub.com/bborbe/agent v0.89.0\n=== final config env block ===\n  env:\n    # Live reads go ONLY through the constrained read-only scripts in agent/scripts/\n    # (read path 1 — task files, read path 2 — metrics). See docs/observation-scripts.md.\n    ALLOWED_TOOLS: \"Read,Grep,Glob,Bash(scripts/vault-read.sh:*),Bash(scripts/vault-list.sh:*),Bash(scripts/prometheus-query.sh:*),Bash(scripts/repo-clone.sh:*)\"\n    LOGLEVEL: \"2\"\n    # LLM auth — fleet norm: stateless token via the in-cluster claude-code-router.\n    ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL: http://claude-code-router-dev:8788\n    ANTHROPIC_MODEL: MiniMax-M2.7-highspeed\n    # The Claude runner strips pod env down to a fixed allowlist (HOME,PATH,USER,TZ,...),\n    # so the read-path endpoints reach the scripts only through this channel: a\n    # comma-separated KEY=VALUE list parsed by both entry points (main.go and\n    # cmd/run-task/main.go). Set as plain pod env they would be dropped before the\n    # model ever sees them.\n    CLAUDE_ENV: \"GIT_REST_URL=http://vault-obsidian-personal:9090,PROMETHEUS_URL=http://prometheus.monitoring:9090\"\n\n  # Holds ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN (router token) — teamvault-resolved, see k8s/defect-diagnoser-agent-secret.yaml (not yet written).\n  secretName: defect-diagnoser-agent\n\n  # Kubernetes API reads, deferred — see NEXT-DIRECTIONS v2. They need a dedicated read-only\n  # ServiceAccount `defect-diagnoser` (get/list on pods, pods/log, events, jobs, deployments;\n=== CHANGELOG ===\n# Changelog\n\n## Unreleased\n\n- feat: Add `agent/scripts/repo-clone.sh`, the fourth read-only observation script, cloning a public GitHub repo into the fixed `repos/` directory beside `scripts/` and reporting `clone_path`, `head_sha` and `default_branch` [rejects any reference that is not `owner/name`, resolves the destination with symlinks followed and refuses anything outside `repos/` before git runs or the filesystem is touched, then makes the clone non-writable]\n- feat: Wire the observation scripts' endpoints through `CLAUDE_ENV` and align the Config allowlist, image and prose with the four scripts that exist [drops the non-existent `pod-logs.sh` entry, adds `git` to the runtime image, and adds `pkg/scripts/consistency_test.go` to fail `make test` when the allowlist, the scripts on disk and the docs disagree]\n\n## v0.0.0\n=== README section ===\n### Claude subprocess env allowlist\n\n`lib/claude/claude-runner.go` strips pod env down to a safe allowlist (`HOME,PATH,USER,TZ,...`) before spawning `claude`, so a variable visible in `kubectl describe pod` can still be absent from the subprocess. Custom env vars (API URLs, credentials) **must** be passed through `CLAUDE_ENV` — a comma-separated `KEY=VALUE` list set on the Config's `spec.env` (or `-claude-env` for a local run) and parsed by both entry points. Don't expect pod env to reach Claude by default.\n\nThe observation scripts get their endpoints this way (contract: `docs/observation-scripts.md`):\n\n`CLAUDE_ENV: \"GIT_REST_URL=http://vault-obsidian-personal:9090,PROMETHEUS_URL=http://prometheus.monitoring:9090\"`\n\n## Local Quick Test","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false}}
